/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFLGPU002 -- laminar flow in a 90 deg planar dividing tee-junction, with
  EVERY linear solve routed through petsc4Foam.

  __MATTYPE__ / __VECTYPE__ are substituted by run_vmflgpu002.sh, exactly as
  VMFLGPU001 and docs/ansys_verification/gpu/smoke_case do:

      GPU arm            : aijcusparse / cuda
      forced-CPU control : aij        / standard

  BOTH ARMS ARE OTHERWISE BYTE-IDENTICAL.  That identity is the entire basis on
  which limb B (|split_GPU - split_CPU|/|split_CPU|) is a statement about WHERE
  the linear algebra ran and about nothing else: same mesh, same schemes, same
  relaxation, same outer loop, same tolerances, same outer iteration count.

  THE OUTER NUMERICS ARE THE CPU PARENT'S, CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER.  VMFL010's
  frozen system/fvSolution carries `consistent yes`, two non-orthogonal
  correctors and relaxation 0.9/0.9, and it is what the parent's MEASURED
  convergence points (729 / 1125 / 1575 SIMPLE iterations at L1/L2/L3,
  VMFL010/RESULTS.md) were obtained under.  Those measurements are this case's
  endTime basis and its cost basis, so changing the outer loop would silently
  invalidate both.  ONLY the linear solvers change -- and the linear solver IS
  the object under verification.

  What changed, and why:
    p : GAMG        -> petsc, ksp_type cg    + pc_type jacobi  (symmetric)
    U : smoothSolver-> petsc, ksp_type bcgs  + pc_type jacobi  (asymmetric)
  The OUTER tolerances (1e-9) and relTol (p 0.01, U 0.1) are the parent's own
  values, unchanged; limb B's 1e-4 bound is derived from them in
  PREREGISTRATION.md section 6.2.

  NO residualControl.  The parent stopped on residualControl, which makes "last
  time == endTime" meaningless; here the run ALWAYS reaches endTime, so rule 4's
  "last time == endTime" and "ExecutionTime count == endTime" clauses bite, and
  BOTH ARMS TAKE THE SAME NUMBER OF OUTER ITERATIONS.  Iterative convergence is
  judged AFTER the run, by the comparator, from the residual history and the
  flow-split plateau.

  NO pRefCell / pRefValue: both outlets carry fixedValue p, so the pressure
  level is set by the boundary conditions and a reference cell would be a second
  specification of an already-determined datum.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      fvSolution;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

solvers
{
    p
    {
        solver          petsc;
        petsc
        {
            options
            {
                ksp_type        cg;
                pc_type         jacobi;
                mat_type        __MATTYPE__;
                vec_type        __VECTYPE__;
            }
            caching { matrix { update always; } preconditioner { update always; } }
        }
        tolerance       1e-9;
        relTol          0.01;
    }

    U
    {
        solver          petsc;
        petsc
        {
            options
            {
                ksp_type        bcgs;
                pc_type         jacobi;
                mat_type        __MATTYPE__;
                vec_type        __VECTYPE__;
            }
            caching { matrix { update always; } preconditioner { update always; } }
        }
        tolerance       1e-9;
        relTol          0.1;
    }
}

SIMPLE
{
    nNonOrthogonalCorrectors 2;
    consistent      yes;
}

relaxationFactors
{
    equations
    {
        U               0.9;
        p               0.9;
    }
}

// ************************************************************************* //
